---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 20, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Dirtybarn handles information on this static site, through Gumroad purchases, and if Google Analytics is enabled in the future."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <section class="store-shell privacy-hero">
    <p class="store-kicker">Privacy</p>
    <div>
      <p class="privacy-hero__date">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
      <h1>A simple site, with a simple data footprint.</h1>
      <p class="privacy-hero__copy">
        Dirtybarn is currently a static website. We do not operate user accounts,
        an on-site checkout, a contact form, a newsletter sign-up, or a visitor
        database on this site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="store-shell privacy-overview" aria-label="Privacy overview">
    <article>
      <p class="store-kicker">On this site / Now</p>
      <h2>No active analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We do not currently run Google Analytics or another marketing tracker on
        this site.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="store-kicker">Purchases</p>
      <h2>Handled by Gumroad</h2>
      <p>
        Checkout, payment, receipts, and digital product delivery take place on
        Gumroad, under Gumroad's own privacy terms.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="store-kicker">Later</p>
      <h2>Analytics, if enabled</h2>
      <p>
        This policy explains what will change if we connect Google Analytics in
        the future.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <div class="store-shell privacy-policy">
    <nav class="privacy-policy__nav" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
      <p class="store-kicker">On this page</p>
      <a href="#information-now">Information handled now</a>
      <a href="#gumroad">Gumroad purchases</a>
      <a href="#analytics">Future analytics</a>
      <a href="#cookies">Cookies</a>
      <a href="#use-and-sharing">Use and sharing</a>
      <a href="#retention">Retention and security</a>
      <a href="#rights">Your rights</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <article class="privacy-policy__content">
      <section id="information-now">
        <p class="store-kicker">01</p>
        <h2>Information handled on this site now</h2>
        <p>
          Dirtybarn does not currently collect account registrations, on-site
          orders, payment details, form submissions, or newsletter subscriptions.
          The site's search feature works in your browser against a public, static
          search index; Dirtybarn does not store your search query in a visitor
          database.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you choose to email us, we receive the email address, message, and any
          information you include. We use it to reply, provide support, discuss a
          license, or respond to your request.
        </p>
        <p>
          Like most websites, the hosting and network providers that deliver and
          protect the site may automatically process limited technical information,
          such as an IP address, request time, browser information, and security
          logs. Their handling of that information is governed by their own terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="gumroad">
        <p class="store-kicker">02</p>
        <h2>Purchases through Gumroad</h2>
        <p>
          Product purchase links take you to Gumroad. Gumroad handles checkout,
          payment processing, receipts, and digital file delivery. It may collect
          contact, transaction, payment, billing, device, and usage information as
          described in its privacy policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          Dirtybarn does not receive or store your full card details on this site.
          Gumroad may provide us with order and customer details needed to deliver a
          purchase, provide customer support, prevent fraud, and meet accounting or
          legal obligations.
        </p>
        <a
          class="privacy-policy__external"
          href="https://gumroad.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
        >Read Gumroad's Privacy Policy ↗</a>
      </section>

      <section id="analytics">
        <p class="store-kicker">03</p>
        <h2>Google Analytics — if enabled later</h2>
        <p>
          Google Analytics is not currently active on this site. If we enable it,
          Google may use cookies or similar technologies to process information such
          as device and browser details, approximate location, referring page, pages
          viewed, interactions, and timestamps.
        </p>
        <p>
          We would use these aggregated insights to understand site performance and
          which content is useful—not to sell your personal information. Where the
          law requires consent, non-essential analytics will be activated only after
          you have been given an appropriate choice.
        </p>
        <div class="privacy-policy__links">
          <a
            class="privacy-policy__external"
            href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >How Google uses information from sites and apps ↗</a>
          <a
            class="privacy-policy__external"
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >Google Privacy Policy ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies">
        <p class="store-kicker">04</p>
        <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
        <p>
          Dirtybarn does not currently set optional analytics or advertising cookies
          on this site. Essential technical storage may still be used by browsers,
          hosting infrastructure, or external services where necessary to provide
          and secure their services.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you follow a link to Gumroad or another external site, that provider
          may use its own cookies under its own policy. If Google Analytics is added,
          we will update the site's consent controls and this policy as needed before
          non-essential analytics cookies are used where consent is required.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="use-and-sharing">
        <p class="store-kicker">05</p>
        <h2>How information is used and shared</h2>
        <p>Where information is handled, we use it only as needed to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>operate, protect, and troubleshoot the website;</li>
          <li>reply to emails and provide product, license, or customer support;</li>
          <li>fulfil and support purchases made through Gumroad;</li>
          <li>meet contractual, accounting, fraud-prevention, or legal duties; and</li>
          <li>understand site performance if analytics is enabled in the future.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell or rent personal information. Information may be handled by
          service providers such as Gumroad, hosting and infrastructure providers,
          and—only if enabled—Google Analytics. We may also disclose information
          where required by law or necessary to protect our rights and users.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention">
        <p class="store-kicker">06</p>
        <h2>Retention and security</h2>
        <p>
          We keep email correspondence and order-related information only for as long
          as reasonably necessary to provide support, manage our business records,
          resolve disputes, and meet legal or accounting requirements. External
          providers set their own retention periods for information they control.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect the
          information available to us. No internet transmission or storage system is
          guaranteed to be completely secure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="rights">
        <p class="store-kicker">07</p>
        <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access,
          correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or objection regarding
          personal information, and to withdraw consent where processing relies on
          consent. You may also have the right to complain to your local data
          protection authority.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contact Dirtybarn for information we control. For information controlled
          directly by Gumroad, Google, or another provider, you may also need to
          contact that provider.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <p class="store-kicker">08</p>
        <h2>Children and policy changes</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly request
          personal information from children through it.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may update this policy when the website, our providers, or applicable
          requirements change. The current version and its last-updated date will be
          published on this page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>

  <section class="store-shell privacy-contact" id="contact" aria-labelledby="privacy-contact-title">
    <p class="store-kicker">Privacy questions</p>
    <div>
      <h2 id="privacy-contact-title">Talk directly to Dirtybarn.</h2>
      <p>
        To ask a question or make a privacy request concerning information controlled
        by Dirtybarn, email us and include enough detail for us to understand your
        request.
      </p>
      <a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:hi@dirtybarn.com?subject=Privacy%20request">
        hi@dirtybarn.com ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
